               12	
               13	## 0. In one paragraph
               14	
               15	Today the menu plays a fixed announcement and that's it. With the assistant we want a short conversation instead: which card, how much is owed and by when, and then two things the caller can get done without waiting for an agent (statement PDF by mail, a different statement week). Paying stays with the agents for now. Whatever else the caller brings up, we hand back to the main menu.
               16	
               17	## 1. Scope
               18	
               19	In:
               20	- Debt reading for one card at a time, all four currencies we carry (Lira, Dollar, Euro, Sterling), with the due date. When the closed statement is fully paid, the "no debt" wording plus the running total.
               21	- The two follow-ups: mailing the statement (only ever to the address we hold) and moving the statement week.
               22	- Choosing the card, where needed.
               23	
               24	Out (first list, Kerem please extend):
               25	- Paying the debt itself: handed to an agent.
               26	- Disputes, "I paid but it doesn't show" (agent, see §7).
               27	- Limits, cash advance, card blocking, anything about debit cards.
               28	- Changing the e-mail address.
               29	- Statements of earlier periods.
               30	
               31	Burcu thinks statement debt is one of the top three menu choices; she'll try to get a figure.
               32	
               33	## 2. How the caller arrives
               34	
               35	The phone menu has already identified and authenticated the caller before the hand-over. The assistant receives the customer number with the call and does not run any identity check of its own.
               36	
               37	**TBD:** the flow drawing we got from the vendor side has a box "second factor may be needed". I don't see why for a read-only step plus two low-risk actions; to confirm with Elçin.
               38	
               39	## 3. Picking the card
               40	
               41	The card list comes from `cards.list` (customer number in, eligible credit cards out). Then:
               42	
               43	| Situation | What the assistant does |
               44	|---|---|
               45	| Caller already named the card when arriving | If the name fits exactly one card, no selection question. |
               46	| Several cards | Asks which one, with at most two example names taken from the caller's own cards: “Hangi kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek istersiniz? Örneğin, Yıldız Premium veya Yıldız Pratik diyebilirsiniz.” |
               47	| Caller asks for "all my cards" | Not possible, the debt service takes one card at a time. Selection question again (counts as a failed attempt). |
               48	| Name not on the list | Tells the caller there is no card with that name and reads the eligible ones again. |
               49	| Two or more cards with the same name | Asks for the last four digits: “Yıldız isimli birden fazla kartınız var. Kartınızın son dört hanesini söyler misiniz?” (name of the card in place of "Yıldız") |
               50	| Same name and same last four | Asks for the full card number: “Son dört hanesi aynı olan birden fazla kartınız var. Kart numaranızın tamamını söyler misiniz?” |
               51	
               52	Two easy cases outside the table: a single card is simply taken, no question. No eligible card at all: “Ekstre borcunu sorgulayabileceğiniz uygun bir kredi kartınız bulunmuyor. Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.”
               53	
               54	Notes:
               55	- Digits can come as "dört iki beş üç", "kırk iki elli üç" etc. The assistant maps them to the four digits and moves on. No reading back of the digits, no "… kartınızla devam ediyorum" confirmation; the card name is said anyway at the start of the debt reading.
               56	- Supplementary card holders: they see no eligible card of their own here. Tell them and ask for a different card. (Burcu, is that what the menu does today?)
               57	- If the card name comes back empty from the service, introduce the card by its last four only.
               58	
               59	## 4. Reading the debt
               60	
               61	Service: `cards.balance` with the chosen card. It returns one block per currency (`debtTL`, `debtUSD`, `debtEUR`, `debtGBP`) with `statementDebt`, `minPayment`, `remainingDebt`, `remainingMinPayment`, `totalDebt`, plus `statementDate`, `lastPayDate`.
               62	
               63	Order:
               64	1. Card introduction + statement date (glued to the first currency).
               65	2. Turkish Lira.
               66	3. Dollar, then Euro, then Sterling (only the ones with debt).
               67	4. One sentence for the currencies with no debt.
               68	5. Remaining auto-payment amount, when there is one (**TBD**, see §9).
               69	6. Due date.
               70	7. If the caller has more eligible cards: “Başka bir kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek ister misiniz?”
