           For anger handling, counting exact replies in code is fragile, so I'd rather handle it via prompt: a system instruction describing up to three calming responses, plus a global "angry_transfer" intent that triggers once conversation context shows the customer is still upset after those calming attempts. Similarly, PIN/OTP volunteering and the third silence case are best handled as prompt-driven rules rather than hardcoded logic.
           
           Since there's no explicit transfer tool in the contract, I'm treating agent transfer as ending the call with an agent flag so the IVR can hand it off.
           
           Now I'm mapping out the different exit nodes — to_agent, to_main_menu, to_login, hangup_silence — and working through service error handling: what lines to show for cards.list returning 500 vs 404, what happens when all cards are supplementary (no eligible card), and similar fallback behavior for balance lookup errors including timeouts. I also need to figure out the right place to show the "checking your info" line relative to when pre_actions and on_enter fire for the balance API node.
           
