           I'm working out how to spell out the year with the correct suffix based on the last spoken word, and getting the last four digits of the card number into spoken form. Then I'm composing the intro sentence for the debt statement, combining the masked card digits, cardholder name, and statement date into a flowing phrase before appending the currency amount.
           
           Now I'm defining the branching logic for the Turkish Lira debt sentence based on remaining debt versus minimum payment -- covering the fully-paid case, the unpaid case, and the partially-paid case, each with distinct phrasing. I'm mirroring this same conditional structure for foreign currency debts like Dollars, starting with the check for whether remaining debt exists.
           
